(version 1)

# 24-pin ATX daughterboard -- 9 blade-tab joints (12V x1 / 5V x2 / 3.3V x1 / 5VSB x1 / GND x4) + a 2x5 signal stub (PWR_OK/PS_ON#/-12V + GND-ref + 6 reserved), standing perpendicular to the main board, tabs blade-down per the owner's 2026-07-05 sketch. Power netclass 0.5mm/0.9-0.5mm via matches the 0.5mm stub tracks laid by route_atx24(); each of the 4 bus rails also gets its own thin In2.Cu lane zone in the corridor below the field (0.3mm wide, 0.65mm pitch -- not netclass-controlled, drawn directly; see ATX24_LANE_SLOT), which the tab row's down-stubs and the field's dodge-stubs meet through 0.3/0.5mm vias.

(rule "Power min width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'Power'"))
